        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Leitneria floridana, Tricyrtis\n- Taxa: Leitneria, lily family\n- Places: Arkansas, Florida, Georgia, Missouri, Texas, southeastern United States, Asia\n\nFacts:\n- Leitneria floridana is the sole species in the genus Leitneria.\n- Leitneria floridana, also called corkwood, is a deciduous dioecious shrub or small tree.\n- Leitneria floridana is found only in the southeastern United States in Arkansas, Florida, Georgia, Missouri, and Texas.\n- Tricyrtis is a genus of Asian flowering plants in the lily family.\n- Tricyrtis has approximately 20 known species.",
